#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Remove idle, clean, fully pushed git worktrees. Fail closed.

A worktree is removed only when every check below passes. Any error, any
unreadable state, or any doubt skips it, and every decision is logged.

  - It is a linked worktree, never a main checkout or a bare repository.
    Scope: every linked worktree registered with a repository found under
    the roots (default ~/code, ~/company and ~/webb), wherever the worktree
    lives; a lane worktree in ~/webb/_wt and one in /tmp are both in scope.
  - It is not locked, and has no merge, rebase, bisect, cherry-pick or revert
    in progress.
  - Nothing in it (files, directories, its index, HEAD and reflogs) changed
    within --idle-hours. Both mtime and ctime count, except the ctime of a
    hardlinked file: pnpm links every node_modules file to its shared store,
    so another checkout's install moves the ctime of files here without
    touching this tree. Until 2026-10-10 that kept every pnpm worktree
    "modified 0.1h ago" and the reaper removed none of beelink2's 343.
  - `git status` shows no tracked change and no untracked file. Ignored
    entries are allowed only when they look like build or dependency output
    (node_modules/, dist/, target/, ...); an ignored .env or notes file skips.
  - It contains no nested git repository or worktree.
  - After `git fetch --all --prune`, every commit reachable from its HEAD is
    reachable from a remote-tracking ref.
  - No process has its cwd, root, an open file or a mapped file inside it
    (/proc on Linux, lsof on macOS). The scan must see every live process,
    so it uses `sudo -n`; if any live process stays unreadable, nothing is
    removed that run.

Removal delegates to the installed `wt-remove`, which owns retention and archive
readback. Only its receipt for the exact, absent checkout confirms removal.
Local branches and other worktree registrations remain intact.

Derived files (--no-derived turns these off). Each pass deletes only what is
rebuilt from tracked inputs or kept in another form, and any doubt keeps it:
  - node_modules: in a linked worktree that was not removed, whose HEAD is in
    the remote default branch or whose pull request at that HEAD is merged or
    closed, untouched for --dependency-idle-hours (default 6), passing the same
    locked, in-progress, mount, nested-repository and process checks. Only
    node_modules directories that git ignores are deleted; changes, untracked
    files and every other path stay.
  - Journey raw recordings: under --journey-state/raw/<journey>-<start>/<label>,
    the .webm files and trace.raw.zip, once journeys/out/<journey>/timings.json
    in a --journey-out directory names that start and out/<journey>/video holds
    <label>-*.mp4 and, for a raw trace, the scrubbed <label>-trace.zip.
  - Linux caches delegate to storage-lifecycle's declared budgets and native GC.
    Beelink-gate itself owns checkout eviction under its existing cache budget.

Reflog expiry rewrites do not count as new work; recorded event times do.

Python 3.9 compatible: macOS runs it with /usr/bin/python3.
"""

